# CODEOWNERS for Kotoba no Takara
#
# What this file does: when a pull request changes a file, GitHub automatically
# asks the owner of the matching path for a review. If several lines match the
# same file, the LAST matching line wins, so general rules come first and
# specific rules come last.
#
# Why every rule is commented out: GitHub accepts only real usernames of
# collaborators with write access. A wrong name shows an error and the rule
# does nothing. The names below (@utilizator-...) are placeholders.
#
# TODO (Kevin): after everyone has accepted the invitation and added their
# username to docs/TEAM.md, replace each placeholder with the real @username
# and remove the "# " at the start of each rule line.
#
# Do NOT turn on "Require review from Code Owners" for main. Most paths have
# one owner, GitHub never lets authors approve their own pull request, and
# main has no admin bypass, so every owner would be blocked on their own
# folder. This file only requests the owner as reviewer automatically; the
# merge rule stays "1 approval from someone who ran the code".
#
# The ownership rules are explained in docs/contracts.md, section 3.

